A||||2||CD||Clean throttle body off or on?... ||||5||
Z||000000||CD||12-03-2000||08:20 PM||||The throttle body on my 1987 is really gummed up and causing some idle problems…  I hope that’s the cause.  Anyway, I’ve read some posts on the subject and I have two questions.<P>1. Is it better to remove the plenum, lower, and upper intake manifold and clean them off the engine or just use the carb. cleaner through the butterfly.<BR>2. If the intake manifold is left on, can the carb. cleaner or the debris that is disolves cause damage to the engine. <P>Thanks for your help.    <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||12-03-2000||08:32 PM||||It's hard to clean the plenums without having them hot tanked. The carbon is tenacious stuff. Certainly, if they are really bad, pull them off. At the same time, there's not much affect from the coating of carbon/EGR fuzz in the upper and lower plenums unless it's horrifying (thick, thick, thick).  <P>As for the TB, it's best to remove it, remove the TPS, IAC, et al and use carb cleaner or a dip. Clean the IAC (idle passage) well. Reinstall the TB using a new gasket and watch the idle hose that goes back down to the lower intake. If it leaks, the idle will be wonky. Cleaning the TB is well worth it. I clean mine every 6 months. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-03-2000||10:31 PM||||.duplicate.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
